  <bioghist id="8f66839cd635ae665712a5b640d31ad8">
    <head>Biographical / Historical</head>
<p>Porter McKeever, joined John D. Rockefeller 3rd's staff in 1973 as a senior advisor after a long career in public administration and international relations.</p><p>McKeever had served as Director of Information of the U.S. Mission to the United Nations from 1946 to 1952.</p><p>In 1953, he was appointed Director of Public Information at the Ford Foundation and served a similar role with the Council for Economic Development.</p><p>In 1964, McKeever founded and became the first president of the United Nations Association of the United States.</p><p>In the late 1980s, McKeever authored a biography of Adlai Stevenson II.</p>  </bioghist>
  <scopecontent id="9f468d9316e8d657f561500ad2538686">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>The collections contains correspondence, memoranda, chronological files and a variety of meeting records, as well as documentation of the long-standing professional contacts and relationships fostered by Porter McKeever and John D. Rockefeller 3rd.</p>  </scopecontent>
  <userestrict id="c0aa12c8c8a15e3b21b9f21783e9c5a1">
